  "note": "A mountain attack by multiple threats on one posn (MW s7 para 13 a pp 83-84): the assault onto the Obj's left flank from its FUP, a fire base on an adjoining hill to the right (long range direct fire weapons, one target per two weapons, MW para 28 p 94), and a Pl of D Coy infiltrating to block the En routes of reinforcement and escape behind the Obj (p 84 (b), (d)). The Obj a hill feature on a flank of the main axis or in the rear that dominates the defences (p 78 para 3); a reserve on this axis, C Coy (p 82 para 9: a central reserve is of little value); P adds phases with liberal timings. Laid on the left flank attack's geometry (IBB p 201 FUP), which the ground notes for mountains qualify (MW pp 83, 85, 228).",
